Date: Thu, 8 Oct 2026 14:16:16 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 1/5] scheduler v2: add the analytic model module
 (scripts/amodel.py)

The existence study's calibrated analytic model (max-entropy local CLT with
exact lattice factors, K_n and kappa calibration) predicts vectors, squares
per sum, P(magic | square), traversal rates and labels per (P, S) with ~3
fitted constants, and was tested on held-out data up to N = 45k, where the
scheduler's regression has no growth beyond N ~ 5.5k. This ports it into the
repo, vectorised over S, with validity guards for the ill-conditioned points
near S_min, the review factors, the N bias correction, the label predictor,
and the label-aware time law (prior refit on the model's own N' and L_raw)
with an online Bayesian-ridge refit.

